  "prompt_sha256": "84bd987816713372e4d8b4ea9621f30e4f02809640ffb1f09716cfe3eda03572",
  "raw_response": "{\"hypothesis\":\"For Phenethylamine with AlPhos, bases that are strongest in the same-substrate sources should transfer best; specifically, a BTTP quality anchor at 100 C with moderate-to-long residence time should outperform non-BTTP alternatives, while one BTMG and one DBU high-temperature long-residence probe test whether AlPhos shifts the optimum away from the BTTP-dominated same-substrate pattern.\",\"selected_candidate_ids\":[\"baumgartner_cn_phenethylamine_alphos_020\",\"baumgartner_cn_phenethylamine_alphos_013\",\"baumgartner_cn_phenethylamine_alphos_014\"],\"selected_source_view\":\"same_substrate\",\"selection_roles\":[{\"candidate_id\":\"baumgartner_cn_phenethylamine_alphos_020\",\"role\":\"quality_anchor\"},{\"candidate_id\":\"baumgartner_cn_phenethylamine_alphos_013\",\"role\":\"complementary_probe\"},{\"candidate_id\":\"baumgartner_cn_phenethylamine_alphos_014\",\"role\":\"complementary_probe\"}],\"mechanism\":\"The strongest transfer signal comes from the same-substrate campaigns, where Phenethylamine with tBuXPhos and tBuBrettPhos is dominated at the top by BTTP under high temperature and moderate-to-long residence times. Candidate 020 is the closest AlPhos analogue to that pattern and is also highly ranked by aggregate source evidence. Because source information disappears after the initial batch, the design should not overconcentrate on one inferred optimum family. Candidate 013 adds a strongly supported same-precatalyst/overall prior: in AlPhos sources, BTMG or DBU at 100 C with longer residence is often strong, and 013 is the top all-sources candidate. Candidate 014 tests the same high-temperature/long-residence region but with DBU, matching the best Aniline-AlPhos observations even more directly. Together these three keep to the source-supported quality region while testing whether substrate identity preserves BTTP preference or whether AlPhos shifts the best base to BTMG/DBU.\",\"confidence\":0.67,\"failure_conditions\":[\"If AlPhos changes the base preference for Phenethylamine so strongly that BTTP is no longer competitive, the anchor will fail.\",\"If the target optimum lies in short-residence or lower-temperature regions not reflected by the selected long-residence 100 C candidates, this initial design will miss it.\",\"If same-precatalyst transfer is more predictive than same-substrate transfer, DBU/BTMG may outperform BTTP and the stated hypothesis is falsified.\",\"If the hidden best base is MTBD or another unselected family, the chosen set undercovers the relevant categorical space.\"],\"abstain\":false,\"abstain_reason\":\"\"}",
  "parsed_response": {
